; The vendored ppx_expect corpus stays byte-identical to upstream, so
; formatting is disabled for the subtree; drive.exe spawns one runner and
; writes a placeholder for every correction it did not produce, so every
; diff rule has a file to compare. See doc/dev/testing.md, "The conformance
; corpus".

(env
 (_
  (formatting disabled)))

(executable
 (name drive)
 (modules drive))

(executable
 (name pp)
 (modules pp)
 (libraries ppxlib ppx_windtrap))
